    skos:definition "A good bought by consumers that tends to last for less than a year. Common examples are food and clothing. The notable thing about nondurable goods is that consumers tend to continue buying them regardless of the ups and downs of the business cycle."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch <http://eurovoc.europa.eu/4880> ;
