<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/1173> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/4350> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00014591>,
        <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Carbon_monoxide> ;
    skos:definition "Colorless, odourless, tasteless, non-corrosive, highly poisonous gas of about the same density as that of air. Very flammable, burning in air with bright blue flame. Although each molecule of CO has one carbon atom and one oxygen atom, it has a shape similar to that of an oxygen molecule (two atoms of oxygen), which is important with regard to it's lethality."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch <http://aims.fao.org/aos/agrovoc/c_1303>,
        <http://rdfdata.eionet.europa.eu/eea/determinants/28> ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Kohlenmonoxid"@de,
        "carbon monoxide"@en .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/11734> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/8204> ;
    skos:definition "A gas at ordinary temperatures; produces an orange-red deposit when cooled to temperatures of liquid air; prepared by passing an electric discharge through a mixture of sulfur vapor and sulfur dioxide at low temperature."@en ;
