<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/1480> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/2457> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Climax_vegetation> ;
    skos:definition "A botanical term referring to the terminal community said to be achieved when a sere (a sequential development of a plant community or group of plant communities on the same site over a period of time) achieves dynamic equilibrium with its environment and in particular with its prevailing climate. Each of the world's major vegetation climaxes is equivalent to a biome. Many botanists believe that climate is the master factor in a plant environment and that even if several types of plant succession occur in an area they will all tend to converge towards a climax form of vegetation."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Klimax"@de,
        "climax"@en .

