    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00100041>,
        <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Antarctica> ;
    skos:definition "A continent lying chiefly within the Antarctic Circle and asymmetrically centered on the South Pole: it consists of an ice-covered plateau (some 95 percent of Antarctica is covered by an icecap averaging 1,6 km in thickness), 1800-3000 m above sea level, and mountains ranges rising to 4500 m with some volcanic peaks; average temperatures all below freezing and human settlement is confined to research station."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch <http://aims.fao.org/aos/agrovoc/c_471>,
        <http://eurovoc.europa.eu/1983> ;
