        "land ecology"@en .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/4623> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/4257> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00006594> ;
    skos:definition "The protective shielding, consisting of soil or some other material, that encloses disposal sites for compacted, non-hazardous solid waste, or secures disposal sites for hazardous waste to minimize the chance of releasing hazardous substances into the environment."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Deponieabdeckung"@de,
        "landfill covering"@en .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/4625> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/3572> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00006602>,
        <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Landfill_gas> ;
    skos:definition "Landfill gas is generated in landfill sites by the anaerobic decomposition of domestic refuse (municipal solid waste). It consists of a mixture of gases and is colourless with an offensive odour due to the traces of organosulphur compounds. Aside for its unpleasantness, it is highly dangerous as methane is explosive in concentrations in air between 5 per cent, the Lower Explosive Limit (LEL), and the Upper Explosive Limit (UEL) of 15 per cent. Landfill gas must be controlled at all operational landfill sites, whether actively or passively vented or both especially in the case of deep sites."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Deponiegas"@de,
        "landfill gas"@en .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/4626> a skos:Concept ;
