<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/4649> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/4648> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00030253> ;
    skos:definition "The process of mining disfigures the surface of the land, and in the absence of reclamation leads to permanent scars. The process spoils the vital topsoil, disrupts drainage patterns, destroys the productive capacity of agricultural and forest land and impairs their aesthetic and social value."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Bergbaufolgelandschaft"@de,
        "landscape after mining"@en .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/465> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/6364> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00100041> ;
    skos:definition "An area within the Antarctic Circle that includes the fifth largest continent and its surrounding waters, consisting mostly of thick ice shelves."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch <http://eurovoc.europa.eu/1983> ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Antarktis"@de,
        "Antarctic region"@en .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/4651> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/538> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00030515>,
        <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Landscape_architecture> ;
    skos:definition "The creation, development, and decorative planting of gardens, grounds, parks, and other outdoor spaces. Landscape gardening is used to enhance nature helping to create a natural setting for individual residences and buildings, and even towns, particularly where special approaches and central settings are required."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Landschaftsarchitektur"@de,
        "landscape architecture"@en .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/4652> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/4648> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00015735> ;
    skos:definition "In visual assessment work, landscapes can be divided into four major elements. a) Form is the perceived mass or shape of an object that appears unified, and which provides a consciousness of its distinction and relation of a whole to the component parts. b) Line is the real or imagined path, border, boundary, or intersection of two planes, such as a silhouette, that the eye follows when perceiving abrupt differences in form, colour or texture. c) Colour is a visual perception that enables the eye to differenciate otherwise identical objects based on the wavelengths of reflected light. d) Texture is the visual feel of a landscape."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Landschaftselement"@de,
        "landscape component"@en .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/4654> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/6376> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00015746> ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Landschaftspflege"@de,
        "landscape conservation policy"@en .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/4657> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/10129> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00015743>,
        <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Landscape_ecology> ;
    skos:definition "The study of landscapes taking account of the ecology of their biological populations. The subjects thus embraces geomorphology and ecology and is applied to the design and architecture of landscapes."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Landschaftsökologie"@de,
        "landscape ecology"@en .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/4659> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/6225> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00015751>,
        <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Landscape_planning> ;
    skos:definition "The aspect of the land use planning process that deals with physical, biological, aesthetic, cultural, and historical values and with the relationships and planning between these values, land uses, and the environment."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Landschaftsplanung"@de,
        "landscape planning"@en .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/4661> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/6743> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00015760> ;
    skos:definition "Area where landscape is protected for its particular features in order to maintain its role in contributing to the wider enjoyment of the countryside."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Landschaftsschutzgebiet"@de,
        "landscape protection area"@en .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/4668> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/3652> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00028791>,
        <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Landslide> ;
    skos:definition "Mass-movement landforms and processes involving the downslope transport, under gravitationary influence of soil and rock material en masse."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Erdrutsch"@de,
        "landslide"@en .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/4680> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/1447> ;
    skos:definition "The arrangement of land units into a variety of categories based on the properties of the land or its suitability for a particular purpose. It has become an important tool in rural land-resource planning."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Flächennutzungsklassifikation"@de,
        "land use classification"@en .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/4684> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/13102> ;
    skos:definition "Type of management and utilization of the soil."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Bodennutzungssystem"@de,
        "soil use regime"@en .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/4686> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/193> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00045830> ;
    skos:definition "The monetary or material worth in commerce or trade of an area of ground considered as property."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Bodenwert"@de,
        "land value"@en ;
    skos:relatedMatch <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Real_estate_appraisal> .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/4698> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/6884> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00015837>,
        <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Laser> ;
    skos:definition "Acronym for Light Amplification by Stimulated Emission of Radiation; a device that produces a powerful, highly directional, monochromatic, coherent beam of light. Laser consist of a transparent cylinder with a reflecting surface at one end and a partially reflecting surface at the other. Light waves are reflected back and forth, some of them emerging at the partially reflecting end. The light source may be a ruby, whose chromium atoms are excited by a flash lamp so that they emit pulses of highly coherent light, or a mixture of inert gases that produce a continuos beam, or a cube of treated gallium arsenide which emits infrared radiation when an electric current passes through it."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch <http://aims.fao.org/aos/agrovoc/c_26026>,
        <http://eurovoc.europa.eu/3874> ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Laser"@de,
        "laser"@en .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/4708> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/13290> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00011254> ;
    skos:definition "An alteration of or addition to any statute with legal force that, if approved by the appropriate legislative authority, supersedes the original statute."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch <http://eurovoc.europa.eu/3703> ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Gesetzesnovellierung"@de,
        "law amendment"@en .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/471> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/6740> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00651200> ;
    skos:definition "Area of protection of the life style of societies where traditional human activities are still maintained and the exploitation of natural resources is still carried out without compromising the future availability."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Anthropologisches Reservat"@de,
        "anthropologic reserve"@en .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/4715> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/6290> ;
    skos:definition "A binding rule or body of rules prescribed by a government to protect human health and the environment, manage growth and development or enhance the quality of life in small geographical and social areas within cities where residents share values and concerns and interact with one another on a daily basis."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Nachbarschaftsrecht"@de,
        "neighbourhood law"@en .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/4719> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/7472> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00020521> ;
    skos:definition "Complex of rules fixed by law or custom which regulate social relations."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch <http://eurovoc.europa.eu/3935> ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Rechtswissenschaft"@de,
        "law (science)"@en ;
    skos:relatedMatch <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Laws_of_science> .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/4722> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/6233> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Leaching> ;
    skos:definition """1) The process of separating a liquid from a solid (as in waste liquid by percolation into the surrounding soil. 
2) Extraction of soluble components of a solid mixture by percolating a solvent through it.
3) To lose or cause to lose soluble substances by the action of a percolating liquid."""@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:narrowMatch <http://aims.fao.org/aos/agrovoc/c_15591> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Auswaschung"@de,
        "leaching"@en .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/4724> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/4350> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00005231>,
        <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Lead_compound> ;
    skos:definition "Lead compounds are present as gasoline additives, in paint, ceramic products, roofing, caulking, electrical applications, tubes, or containers. Lead exposure may be due to air, water, food, or soil. Lead in the air is primarily due to lead-based fuels and the combustion of solid waste, coal, oils, and emissions from alkyl lead manufacturers, wind blown dust volcanoes, the burning of lead-painted surfaces, and cigarette smoke. Lead in drinking water comes from leaching from lead pipes, connectors, and solder in both the distribution system and household plumbing."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Bleiverbindung"@de,
        "lead compound"@en .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/4725> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/11676> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00050625> ;
    skos:definition "The presence and release into the air, water and soil, of lead, a toxic metal used in plumbing, gasoline and lead-acid batteries."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch <http://eurovoc.europa.eu/3162> ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Bleiverseuchung"@de,
        "lead contamination"@en .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/4727> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/4247> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00004322> ;
    skos:definition "A binding rule or body of rules prescribed by a government to reduce or eliminate the lead content in petroleum fuels used in vehicular and other engines that pollute the air with lead-carrying exhaust."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Benzinbleigesetz"@de,
        "lead-in-petrol law"@en .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/4728> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/6359> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00005261> ;
    skos:definition "A measure of the amount of lead or lead salts absorbed by the body as a possible sign of acute or chronic lead poisoning, which can affect the nervous, digestive or muscular systems."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Blutbleispiegel"@de,
        "lead level in blood"@en .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/4730> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/6300> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Leaf> ;
    skos:definition "The main organ of photosynthesis and transpiration in higher plants, usually consisting of a flat green blade attached to the stem directly or by a stalk."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Blatt (Pflanze)"@de,
        "leaf"@en .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/4735> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/442> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00015972>,
        <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Leather> ;
    skos:definition "The dressed or tanned hide of an animal, usually with the hair removed."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch <http://aims.fao.org/aos/agrovoc/c_4241>,
        <http://eurovoc.europa.eu/315> ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Leder"@de,
        "leather"@en .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/4738> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/4279> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00015979> ;
    skos:definition "Industry for the production of leather goods such as garments, bags, etc."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch <http://aims.fao.org/aos/agrovoc/c_4242>,
        <http://eurovoc.europa.eu/1388> ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Lederindustrie"@de,
        "leather industry"@en .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/4739> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/13288> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00020478> ;
    skos:definition "The fundamental law or judicial precedent that warrants or supports a subsequent decision or action by any governmental, corporate or private entity."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch <http://eurovoc.europa.eu/5456> ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Rechtsgrundlage"@de,
        "legal basis"@en .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/474> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/4154> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00002342>,
        <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Antibody> ;
    skos:definition "A complex protein that is produced in response to the introduction of a specific antigen into an animal. Antibodies belong to a class of proteins called immunoglobins, which are formed by plasma cells in the blood as a defence mechanism against invasion by parasites, notably bacteria and viruses, either by killing them or rendering them harmless."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Antikörper"@de,
        "antibody"@en .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/4741> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/111> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00020480> ;
    skos:definition "A justifiable claim to have or obtain something or to act in a certain way, which is supported by law and is covered or shielded from the danger of being revoked or repealed."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch <http://eurovoc.europa.eu/6106> ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Rechtsgut"@de,
        "legally protected right"@en .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/4743> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/11514> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00020515> ;
    skos:definition "Any order or rule issued by a government stipulating its procedures for the creation, execution or adjudication of laws."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Rechtsverordnung"@de,
        "legal regulation"@en .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/4744> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/13288> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00020467>,
        <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Legal_remedy> ;
    skos:definition "The means by which a right is enforced or the violation of a right is prevented, redressed, or compensated."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Rechtsbehelf"@de,
        "legal remedy"@en .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/4746> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/13288> ;
    skos:definition "The exact wording or language of a law or other document in conformity with the law or having the authority of law."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Rechtsdokument"@de,
        "legal text"@en ;
    skos:relatedMatch <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Fine_print> .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/475> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/7236> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00010646> ;
    skos:definition "The act of foreseeing, expecting and taking measures against possible future exposure to harm, death or a thing that causes these."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Gefahrenvorsorge"@de,
        "anticipation of danger"@en .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/4758> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/2862> ;
    skos:definition "A binding rule or body of rules prescribed by a government to manage and protect an area's natural water supply and waterways."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Wasserressourcenrecht"@de,
        "water resources legislation"@en .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/4759> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/661> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00011263> ;
    skos:definition "The power of a deliberative assembly of persons or delegates to bring a bill, resolution or special act to an official, legally binding status."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Gesetzgeber"@de,
        "legislative authority"@en .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/4760> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/103> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00011269> ;
    skos:definition "The skill, knowledge, qualification, capacity or authority to make, give or enact rules with binding force upon a population or jurisdiction."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch <http://eurovoc.europa.eu/2586> ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Gesetzgebungskompetenz"@de,
        "legislative competence"@en .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/4762> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/6801> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00050631> ;
    skos:definition "Knowledge or a service providing knowledge concerning actual and proposed laws, including approval status, the history and content of deliberative proceedings and the specific language of those laws."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Gesetzesinformation"@de,
        "legislative information"@en .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/4764> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/10833> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00015991>,
        <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Legislature> ;
    skos:definition "The department, assembly, or body of persons that makes statutory laws for a state or nation."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch <http://eurovoc.europa.eu/2586> ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Legislative"@de,
        "legislature"@en .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/4784> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/8308> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00000409>,
        <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Levy> ;
    skos:definition "A ratable portion of the produce of the property and labor of the individual citizens, taken by the nation, in the exercise of its sovereign rights, for the support of government, for the administration of the laws, and as the means for continuing in operation the various legitimate functions of the state."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Abgabe"@de,
        "levy"@en .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/4785> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/2286> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00016129>,
