<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/5415> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/4629> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00040244> ;
    skos:definition "A relatively level area of fine silt along a shore (as in a sheltered estuary) or around an island, alternately covered and uncovered by the tide, or covered by shallow water."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Schlickwatt"@de,
        "mud flat"@en ;
    skos:relatedMatch <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Mudflat> .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/5417> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/7565> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Mud> ;
    skos:definition "A mixture of clay and/or silt with water to form a plastic mass with a particle size preponderantly below 0.06 mm diameter. It is deposited in low-energy environments in lakes, estuaries and lagoons. It may also be deposited in deep-sea environments."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Schlamm (Sediment)"@de,
        "mud (sediment)"@en .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/5418> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/5510> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Mulch> ;
    skos:definition "A layer of organic material applied to the surface of the ground to retain moisture; mulching is the spreading of leaves, straw or other loose material on the ground to prevent erosion, evaporation or freezing of plant roots."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Mulch"@de,
        "mulch"@en .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/5419> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/4417> ;
    skos:definition "Multilateralism stands for a long-held but rarely achieved ideal, namely the voluntary co-operation of nations for peace and development. Multilateral initiatives are undermined or diluted by ultra-nationalist, bilateral and regional initiatives. Multilateralism may be undercut by the uncoordinated decisions of those contributing to it. Multilateralism constitutes the democracy of international society. An enlightened multilateralism enhances the specific interests of states while advancing their common cause."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch <http://eurovoc.europa.eu/3463> ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Multilaterales Abkommen"@de,
        "multilateral agreement"@en ;
    skos:relatedMatch <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Multilateral_treaty> .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/5421> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/3232> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00017600> ;
