<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/7046> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/6740> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Refuge> ;
    skos:definition "A restricted and isolated area in which plants and animals persisted during a period of continental climatic change that made surrounding areas uninhabitable; especially an ice-free or unglaciated area within or close to a continental ice sheet or upland ice cap, where hardy biotas eked out an existence during a glacial phase. It later served as a center of dispersal for the repopulation of surrounding areas after climatic readjustment."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Refugium"@de,
        "refuge"@en .

