    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00005066>,
        <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Bioluminescence> ;
    skos:definition "The production of light of various colors by living organisms (e.g. some bacteria and fungi, glow-worms and many marine animals). Luminescence is produced by a biochemical reaction, which is catalyzed by an enzyme. In some animals the light is used as a mating signal; in others it may be a protective device. In deep-sea forms luminous organs may serve as lanterns."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Biolumineszenz"@de,
        "bioluminescence"@en .

