<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/8875> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/2749> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00005655> ;
    skos:definition "Calorific value is the heat per unit mass produced by complete combustion of a given substance. Calorific values are used to express the energy values of fuels; usually these are expressed in megajoules per kilogram. They are also used to measure the energy content of foodstuffs; i.e. the energy produced when the food is oxidized in the body. The units here are kilojoules per gram. Calorific values are measured using a bomb calorimeter (apparatus consisting of a strong container in which the sample is sealed with excess oxygen and ignited electrically. The heat of combustion at constant volume can be calculated from the resulting rise in temperature)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Brennwertnutzung"@de,
        "utilisation of calorific value"@en .

