    skos:relatedMatch <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Pump> .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/921> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/7298> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00005148>,
        <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Bitumen> ;
    skos:definition "A generic term applied to natural inflammable substances of variable colour, hardness, and volatility, composed principally of a mixture of hydrocarbons substantially free from oxygenated bodies. Bitumens are sometimes associated with mineral matter, the nonmineral constituents being fusible and largely soluble in carbon disulfide, yielding water-insoluble sulfonation products. Petroleum, asphalts, natural mineral waxes, and asphaltites are all considered bitumens."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch <http://aims.fao.org/aos/agrovoc/c_26896> ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Bitumen"@de,
        "bitumen"@en .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/9211> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/6842> ;
    skos:definition "Plant where water, through physical and chemical processes, is made suitable for human consumption and other purposes."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Wasserreinigungsanlage"@de,
        "water purification plant"@en .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/9217> a skos:Concept ;
