<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/2477> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broadMatch <http://eurovoc.europa.eu/2724> ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/2810> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00018491> ;
    skos:definition "The competency in performance in business matters involving the relation between financial and environmental principles."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Ökonomisch-ökologische Effizienz"@de,
        "economical-ecological efficiency"@en ;
    skos:related <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/15329> .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/2497> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/6287> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Economic_planning> ;
    skos:definition "An economy in which prices, incomes etc. are determined centrally by government rather than through the operation of the free market, and in which industrial production is governed by an overall national plan."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch <http://eurovoc.europa.eu/2402> ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Wirtschaftsplanung"@de,
        "economic planning"@en .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/2505> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/2476> ;
    skos:definition "The complex of elements which, in a given period, characterize the condition or state of a country or region's ability to produce goods, services and other resources with exchange value."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch <http://aims.fao.org/aos/agrovoc/c_28674>,
        <http://eurovoc.europa.eu/5146> ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Ökonomische Situation"@de,
        "economic situation"@en ;
    skos:related <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/15131> .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/2510> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/2501> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00027911> ;
    skos:definition "The study of relationships in the economy. Its purpose is to analyze and explain the behaviour of the various economic elements. The body of economic theory can be divided into two broad categories, positive theory and welfare theory. Positive theory is an attempt to analyze the operation of the economy without considering the desirability of its results in terms of ultimate goals. Welfare theory is concerned primarily with an evaluation of the economic system in terms of ethical goals which are not themselves derived from economic analysis."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Wirtschaftstheorie"@de,
        "economic theory"@en ;
    skos:relatedMatch <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Economics> .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/2527> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/8522> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00050001>,
        <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Ecotourism> ;
    skos:definition "Excursions to relatively untouched lands, which for the tourist promise the chance to observe unusual wildlife and indigenous inhabitants. The travel industry, in an attempt to market adventure and authenticity to those travellers weary of \"civilisation\" promote travel to environments free of modern technology. Ecotourism's inherent contradiction is the promotion of untouched lands, which immediately become touched by the hands of tourism."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Ökotourismus"@de,
        "ecotourism"@en ;
    skos:related <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/15309> .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/2536> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/2534> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00041250> ;
    skos:definition "Regulation designed to identify and control of risks deriving from existing chemicals. According to this program the main goal is the collection of basic information about existing chemicals including their uses and characteristics, environmental fate and pathways, toxicity and ecotoxicity."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "EU-Altstoffverordnung"@de,
        "EC regulation on existing chemicals"@en ;
    skos:related <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/3047> .

