    skos:definition "Tropospheric ozone is a secondary pollutant formed from emissions of nitrogen oxides, non-methane volatile organic compounds and carbon monoxide. Ozone scars lung tissue, makes eyes sting and throats itch. It has been implicated as a contributor to forest dieback, damage to agricultural crops, etc."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch <http://aims.fao.org/aos/agrovoc/c_35254> ;
