<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/2400> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/4855> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00008540> ;
    skos:definition "The outer layers of the Earth's structure, varying between 6 and 48 km in thickness, and comprising all the material above the Mohorovicic Discontinuity (a seismic discontinuity occurring between the crust of the earth and the underlying mantle; the discontinuity occurs at an average depth of 35 km below the continents and at about 10 km below the oceans). The earlier idea of a cool solid skin overlaying a hot molten interior has now been replaced by a concept of a crust composed of two shells: an inner basic unit composed of sima (oceanic crust) and an outer granitic unit composed of sial (continental crust)."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Erdkruste"@de,
        "earth's crust"@en ;
    skos:relatedMatch <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Crust_%28geology%29> .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/2470> a skos:Concept ;
