    skos:definition "The art and science of designing and building structures, or large groups of structures, in keeping with aesthetic and functional criteria."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch <http://eurovoc.europa.eu/2471> ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Architektur"@de,
        "architecture"@en .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/5494> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/4599> ;
    skos:definition "An area in which natural processes predominate, fluctuations in numbers of organisms are allowed free play and human intervention is minimal."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Naturgebiet"@de,
        "natural area"@en ;
    skos:related <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/15335> .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/5496> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/2215> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00028887>,
        <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Natural_disaster> ;
    skos:definition "Violent, sudden and destructive change in the environment without cause from human activity, due to phenomena such as floods, earthquakes, fire and hurricanes."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch <http://aims.fao.org/aos/agrovoc/c_10391> ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Naturkatastrophe"@de,
        "natural disaster"@en ;
    skos:related <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/12849> .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/5500> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/3169> ;
    skos:definition "Organic material added to the soil to supply chemical elements needed for plant nutrition."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Naturdünger"@de,
        "natural fertiliser"@en ;
    skos:related <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/15168> .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/5545> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/10201> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00017898>,
        <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Nature_reserve> ;
    skos:definition "Areas allocated to preserve and protect certain animals and plants, or both. They differ from national park, which are largely a place for public recreation, because they are provided exclusively to protect species for their own sake. Endangered species are increasingly being kept in nature reserves to prevent them from extinction, particularly in India, Indonesia and some African countries. Natural reserves were used once to preserve the animals that landowners hunted, but, in the 19th century, they became places where animals were kept to prevent them from dying out. Special refuges and sanctuaries are also often designated to protect certain species or groups of wild animals or plants, especially if their numbers and distribution have been significantly reduced. They also serve as a place for more plentiful species to rest, breed or winter. Many parts of the world also have marine and aquatic reserves to protect different species of sea or freshwater plant and animal life."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch <http://aims.fao.org/aos/agrovoc/c_16141> ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Naturschutzgebiet"@de,
        "nature reserve"@en ;
    skos:related <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/10032> .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/5605> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/2640> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00023460>,
        <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Nitrogen> ;
    skos:definition "An essential nutrient in the food supply of plants and the diets of animals. Animals obtain it in nitrogen-containing compounds, particularly amino acids. Although the atmosphere is nearly 80% gaseous nitrogen, very few organisms have the ability to use it in this form. The higher plants normally obtain it from the soil after micro-organisms have converted the nitrogen into ammonia or nitrates, which they can then absorb."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch <http://aims.fao.org/aos/agrovoc/c_5192>,
        <http://eurovoc.europa.eu/4545> ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Stickstoff"@de,
        "nitrogen"@en .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/5613> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/4350> ;
    skos:definition "Oxides formed and released in all common types of combustion; they are formed by the oxidation of atmospheric nitrogen at high temperatures. Introduced into the atmosphere from car exhausts, furnace stacks, incinerators, power stations and similar sources, the oxides include nitrous oxide, nitric oxide, nitrogen dioxide, nitrogen pentoxide and nitric acid. The oxides of nitrogen undergo many reactions in the atmosphere to form photochemical smog."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch <http://aims.fao.org/aos/agrovoc/c_16002> ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Stickstoffoxide"@de,
        "nitrogen oxides"@en ;
    skos:related <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/3572> ;
    skos:relatedMatch <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Nitrogen_oxide> .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/5674> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/6884> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00018059> ;
    skos:definition "Radiation that does not change the structure of atoms but does heat tissue and may cause harmful biological effects."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch <http://eurovoc.europa.eu/6747> ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Nichtionisierende Strahlung"@de,
        "non-ionising radiation"@en ;
    skos:relatedMatch <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Non-ionizing_radiation> .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/5686> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/1029> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00051721> ;
    skos:definition "Area which provides commercial, industrial, and public facilities."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Nichtwohngebäude"@de,
        "non-residential building"@en ;
    skos:related <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/4062> .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/5708> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/4971> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00014243> ;
    skos:definition "An event occurring in a nuclear power plant or anywhere that radioactive materials are used, stored, or transported and involving the release of potentially dangerous levels of radioactive materials into the environment."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch <http://eurovoc.europa.eu/921> ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Kerntechnischer Unfall"@de,
        "nuclear accident"@en ;
    skos:related <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/12793>,
        <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/6887>,
        <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/6904> ;
    skos:relatedMatch <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Nuclear_and_radiation_accidents> .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/5742> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/6977> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00014232> ;
    skos:definition "Device which creates heat and energy by starting and controlling atomic fission."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch <http://eurovoc.europa.eu/2903> ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Kernreaktor"@de,
        "nuclear reactor"@en ;
    skos:related <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/12816>,
        <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/5724>,
        <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/6978> ;
    skos:relatedMatch <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Nuclear_reactor_technology> .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/5831> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/4052> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00018575> ;
    skos:definition "The disaster caused by the dumping and accidental spillage of oil into waterways from ships and land-based or offshore installations. Oil pollution may destroy or damage aquatic life and wildlife such as birds, contaminate water supplies and create fire hazards."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Ölunfall"@de,
        "oil disaster"@en ;
    skos:related <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/5830>,
        <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/5837>,
        <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/5839>,
        <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/5852> .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/5834> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/3087> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00008552> ;
    skos:definition "Recovery of oil by surface mining, as in tar sands or oil shales, or from tunnels in a shallow reservoir."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch <http://eurovoc.europa.eu/3765> ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Erdölförderung"@de,
        "oil extraction"@en ;
    skos:related <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/12488>,
        <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/5836>,
        <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/6161> ;
    skos:relatedMatch <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Extraction_of_petroleum> .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/5837> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/10048> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00018584> ;
    skos:definition "Contamination of any ecosystem, but usually of freshwater or marine ecosystems, by oil or other petroleum products."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch <http://eurovoc.europa.eu/3161> ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Ölverschmutzung"@de,
        "oil pollution"@en ;
    skos:related <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/5827>,
        <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/5831> ;
    skos:relatedMatch <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Oil_spill> .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/5991> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broadMatch <http://eurovoc.europa.eu/2214> ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/5982> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00018829>,
        <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Ozone> ;
    skos:definition "An allotropic form of oxygen containing three atoms in the molecule. It is a bluish gas, very active chemically, and a powerful oxidizing agent. Ozone is formed when oxygen or air is subjected to a silent electric discharge. It occurs in ordinary air in very small amounts only."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch <http://aims.fao.org/aos/agrovoc/c_5485>,
        <http://eurovoc.europa.eu/2215> ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Ozon"@de,
        "ozone"@en ;
    skos:related <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/632>,
        <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/8696> .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/6138> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/5914> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00028746>,
        <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Pest> ;
    skos:definition "Any organism that damages crops, injures or irritates livestock or man, or reduces the fertility of land."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Schädling"@de,
        "pest"@en .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/6139> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/1874> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00028744>,
        <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Pest_control> ;
    skos:definition "Keeping down the number of pests by killing them or preventing them from attacking."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch <http://aims.fao.org/aos/agrovoc/c_5726>,
        <http://eurovoc.europa.eu/4490> ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Schädlingsbekämpfung"@de,
        "pest control"@en .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/6201> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/1324> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00019321> ;
    skos:definition "Chemical reaction which is initiated by light of a specific wavelength. In an environmental context an example is the potential action of ultraviolet light on CFCs which may bring about the detrimental degradation of the ozone layer. Photochemical reactions initiate the process of photosynthesis in which plants convert carbon dioxide into sugars, which are incorporated into cell materials."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Photochemische Reaktion"@de,
        "photochemical reaction"@en ;
    skos:related <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/6211> ;
    skos:relatedMatch <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Photochemistry> .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/6225> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/2889> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00020355> ;
    skos:definition "A form of urban land use planning which attempts to achieve an optimal spatial coordination of different human activities for the enhancement of the quality of life."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Raumplanung"@de,
        "physical planning"@en ;
    skos:related <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/7075> .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/6240> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/881> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00019365>,
        <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Physiology> ;
    skos:definition "The biological study of the functions of living organisms and their parts."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch <http://aims.fao.org/aos/agrovoc/c_49881> ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Physiologie"@de,
        "physiology"@en .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/627> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/641> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00002855> ;
    skos:definition "Any one of a number of strata or layers of the earth's atmosphere; temperature distribution is the most common criterion used for denoting the various shell. Also known as atmospheric shell; atmospheric region."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Atmosphärische Schichtung"@de,
        "atmospheric layering"@en ;
    skos:related <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/4473> .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/6316> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/6240> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00019174>,
        <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Plant_physiology> ;
    skos:definition "The study of the function and chemical reactions within the various organs of plants."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch <http://aims.fao.org/aos/agrovoc/c_25189> ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Pflanzenphysiologie"@de,
        "plant physiology"@en ;
    skos:related <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/6244>,
        <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/6304>,
        <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/971> .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/632> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/623> ;
    skos:definition "A triatomic molecule of oxygen; a natural constituent of the atmosphere, with the highest concentrations in the ozone layer or stratosphere; it is found at a level between 15 and 30 km above the Earth, which prevents harmful ultraviolet B radiation, which causes skin cancer and threatens plant life, from reaching the ground. The fragile shield is being damaged by chemicals released on Earth. The main chemicals that are depleting stratospheric ozone are chlorofluorocarbons (CFCs), which are used in refrigerators, aerosols and as cleaners in many industries and halons, which are used in fire extinguishers. The damage is caused when these chemicals release highly reactive forms of chlorine and bromine."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Atmosphärisches Ozon"@de,
        "atmospheric ozone"@en ;
    skos:related <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/15195>,
        <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/5991> .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/6359> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/4046> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00026036>,
        <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Poisoning> ;
    skos:definition "The morbid condition produced by a poison which may be swallowed, inhaled, injected, or absorbed through the skin."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch <http://aims.fao.org/aos/agrovoc/c_6051> ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:narrowMatch <http://eurovoc.europa.eu/5689> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Vergiftung"@de,
        "poisoning"@en ;
    skos:related <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/8538> .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/636> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/2895> ;
    skos:definition "The presence in the air of one or more contaminants in such a concentration and of such duration as to cause a nuisance or to be injurious to human life, animal life or vegetation."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch <http://eurovoc.europa.eu/2527> ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Atmosphärische Verunreinigung"@de,
        "atmospheric pollution"@en ;
    skos:related <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/7760> ;
    skos:relatedMatch <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Air_pollution> .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/6400> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/2774> ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Schadstoffbewertung"@de,
        "pollutant assessment"@en ;
    skos:related <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/1332>,
        <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/15207>,
        <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/3853>,
        <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/6402> .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/641> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/617> ;
    skos:definition "The gaseous area surrounding the planet is divided into several concentric spherical strata (layers, like shells) separated by narrow transition zones. The boundaries are know as \"pause\". More than 99% of the total atmospheric mass is concentrated in the first 40 km from the Earth's surface. Atmospheric layers are characterized by differences in chemical composition that produce variations in temperature."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Atmosphärischer Aufbau"@de,
        "atmospheric structure"@en .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/6412> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/6395> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00021482> ;
    skos:definition "The process of completely removing a pollutant's source as well as the pollutant itself."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Schadstoffelimination"@de,
        "pollutant elimination"@en ;
    skos:related <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/2015> .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/6459> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/2562> ;
    skos:definition "The main pollution effects concern human health and cover all aspects of the physical environment - air, water and land, including the effects of climate change. Human activities which are sources of pollution arise from domestic, commercial, industrial and military sectors and their effects are influenced by various issues, trends and public sector programmes, such as safe water and food, management of waste, increasing use of chemicals in agriculture, and urbanization. Types of pollutants which are negatively impacting health include litter, toxic chemicals, nuclear waste, lead, spoil from mining, food and water contaminants; and the polluting effects of over-population."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Auswirkung der Verunreinigung"@de,
        "pollution effect"@en .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/6861> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/7784> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00015948>,
        <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Quality_of_life> ;
    skos:definition "Quality of life is largely a matter of individual preference and perception and overlaps the concept of social well-being. Generally the emphasis is on the amount and distribution of jointly consumed public goods, such as health care and welfare services, protection against crime, regulation of pollution, preservation of fine landscapes and historic townscapes."@en ;
    skos:exactMatch <http://aims.fao.org/aos/agrovoc/c_28759>,
        <http://eurovoc.europa.eu/2870> ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Lebensqualität"@de,
        "quality of life"@en .

<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/7003> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:broader <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/3770> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00008662> ;
