<http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/concept/4124> a skos:Concept ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://data.uba.de/umt/_00013003>,
        <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Hydrosphere> ;
    skos:definition "The waters of the Earth, as distinguished from the rocks (lithosphere), living things (biosphere), and the air (atmosphere). Includes the waters of the ocean; rivers, lakes, and other bodies of surface water in liquid form on the continents; snow, ice, and glaciers; and liquid water, ice, and water vapour in both the unsaturated and saturated zones below the land surface. Included by some, but excluded by others, is water in the atmosphere , which includes water vapour, clouds, and all forms of precipitation while still in the atmosphere."@en ;
    skos:inScheme <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> ;
    skos:prefLabel "Hydrosphäre"@de,
        "hydrosphere"@en ;
    skos:topConceptOf <http://www.eionet.europa.eu/gemet/gemetThesaurus> .

